import{_ as t,o as a,c as i,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 850 | Transcended Ones and Art | The Transcended One's Architecture and Spatial Art","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 850 | Transcended Ones and Art | The Transcended One's Architecture and Spatial Art","no":850,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Architecture","Spatial Art","Symbiosis Aesthetics","Habitable Environment"],"related":["39-Housing and Environment Guarantee","46-Environmental Protection Law","64-Isolation-Space Construction Technology","846-Transcended-One Artistic Creation Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0850_模块4-超脱者与艺术-建筑与空间艺术.md","filePath":"en/0850_模块4-超脱者与艺术-建筑与空间艺术.md"}`),o={name:"en/0850_模块4-超脱者与艺术-建筑与空间艺术.md"};function r(s,e,l,c,d,h){return a(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-850-transcended-ones-and-art-the-transcended-one-s-architecture-and-spatial-art" tabindex="-1">Entry 850 | Transcended Ones and Art | The Transcended One&#39;s Architecture and Spatial Art <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-850-transcended-ones-and-art-the-transcended-one-s-architecture-and-spatial-art" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 850 | Transcended Ones and Art | The Transcended One&#39;s Architecture and Spatial Art&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 39, 46, 64, 846</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-what-kind-of-space-people-live-in-they-grow-into" tabindex="-1">Introduction: what kind of space people live in, they grow into <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-what-kind-of-space-people-live-in-they-grow-into" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: what kind of space people live in, they grow into&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s architectural art is power&#39;s monument. The strong build heaven-reaching imperial palaces, towering into clouds, reminding Myriad Ranks &quot;who is master&quot;; ordinary beings cram in dilapidated corners, not even having a cultivation room. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s architectural art is the opposite — it is not &quot;displaying power,&quot; but <strong>&quot;settling Myriad Ranks.&quot;</strong> Public cultivation halls, Myriad-Rank deliberation domes, symbiosis gardens, isolation spaces and anchor hubs; the transcended one lays his understanding of the cosmos and goodwill toward Myriad Ranks together into every brick, every stone, every law, every barrier. This entry explains: how the transcended one makes architecture and spatial art into a symbiotic civilization&#39;s material poetry.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: <strong>the republican axiom of Myriad Races</strong> requires space open to all Myriad-Rank beings, not only building palaces for the strong; <strong>the anti-predation axiom</strong> requires spatial resources not be monopolized by a few; <strong>the collective ascension axiom</strong> requires spatial design serve cultivation and co-building; <strong>the causal self-discipline axiom</strong> requires spatial construction low-pollution, not damaging existing ecosystems; <strong>the law-first axiom</strong> requires spatial law structure be self-consistent, isolation barriers and other technical parameters stable and reusable.</p><p>Among them, <strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong> is the sixth pillar: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. The old cosmos&#39; resources and Great Dao are limited, necessarily leading to predatory involution; the Anchor Symbiotic everyone inherently possesses infinite origin, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-architecture-is-philosophy-how-space-shapes-people" tabindex="-1">I. Architecture Is Philosophy: How Space Shapes People <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-architecture-is-philosophy-how-space-shapes-people" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Architecture Is Philosophy: How Space Shapes People&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou believes space is not only a container, it shapes those who live in it. A space separated by high walls, open only to the strong, teaches people &quot;privilege is a matter of course&quot;; a space open to Myriad Ranks, with traces of &quot;co-building&quot; everywhere, teaches people &quot;we are one.&quot; Therefore the transcended one treats architecture as <strong>public philosophy&#39;s materialization</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Open public cultivation halls</strong>: every plane has free cultivation places, symbolizing &quot;the road is open to all&quot;;</li><li><strong>Myriad-Rank deliberation dome</strong>: representatives of each clan sit equally together, no throne high up — the space itself declares republicanism;</li><li><strong>Symbiosis garden</strong>: ecological space shared by Myriad-Rank plant spirits and material clans, symbolizing ecological symbiosis;</li><li><strong>Anchor hub</strong>: public node for cross-plane traffic and information, symbolizing connection and sharing.</li></ul><h2 id="ii-spatial-art-and-function-united" tabindex="-1">II. Spatial Art and Function United <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-spatial-art-and-function-united" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Spatial Art and Function United&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s architecture is never &quot;beauty for beauty&#39;s sake&quot;; it is beauty and function united:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Space Type</th><th>Aesthetic Expression</th><th>Function</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Public cultivation hall</td><td>Harmony of light and energy flow</td><td>Free cultivation, off-track recovery</td></tr><tr><td>Deliberation dome</td><td>Circular, no throne</td><td>Myriad-Rank democratic consultation</td></tr><tr><td>Symbiosis garden</td><td>Myriad-Rank species coexist</td><td>Ecology, healing, culture</td></tr><tr><td>Isolation space</td><td>Order beauty of seven law barriers</td><td>Safe experiments, low-pollution research</td></tr><tr><td>Cross-plane anchor hub</td><td>Vast beauty of connection</td><td>Cross-plane traffic and communications</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Isolation space&#39;s (Document 64) seven barriers become here a kind of &quot;order beauty&quot; — its beauty is not in ornateness, but in its reliability, its protection of Myriad Ranks. <strong>The highest architectural beauty is that it steadily shelters those who live in it.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-spatial-equality-do-not-build-imperial-palaces" tabindex="-1">III. Spatial Equality: Do Not Build &quot;Imperial Palaces&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-spatial-equality-do-not-build-imperial-palaces" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Spatial Equality: Do Not Build &quot;Imperial Palaces&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one explicitly opposes building ostentatious space for himself:</p><ul><li>Do not build a &quot;heaven-reaching imperial palace&quot; for the transcended one — his dwelling is same-tier as Myriad Ranks, not higher;</li><li>Public space takes priority over private space: first build cultivation halls, deliberation domes, symbiosis gardens, then talk about residence;</li><li>Do not waste resources on buildings that &quot;make the strong look impressive&quot; — that is entry 740&#39;s criticized energy waste.</li></ul><p>This forms a fundamental contrast with the old world&#39;s &quot;build high terraces to overlook Myriad Ranks.&quot; <strong>The true transcended one hopes his own space is unobtrusive — because Myriad Ranks&#39; spaces are all equally good.</strong></p><h2 id="iv-space-and-environmental-responsibility" tabindex="-1">IV. Space and Environmental Responsibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-space-and-environmental-responsibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Space and Environmental Responsibility&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Architecture is not cost-free. Heng Yuan Zhou is bound by the Environmental Protection Law (Document 46):</p><ul><li>Spatial construction low-pollution, does not damage existing plane ecosystems;</li><li>Cross-plane site selection follows Replication Mirror + isolation-space process, does not pollute new planes;</li><li>Abandoned spaces destroyed per standard, leaving no residue (consistent with entry 844).</li></ul><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: public-space priority, reject ostentatious architecture, use resources where Myriad Ranks truly need them</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: space open to Myriad Ranks, do not build imperial palaces, sealing predatory aesthetics of &quot;flaunting power with architecture&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: the Tang-Luo system&#39;s strong ones build imperial palaces, looking down from above; Heng Yuan Zhou builds open public spaces, dwelling with Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: spaces designed per five-lineage life forms; plant spirits, consciousness-information clans all have adapted venues</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: spatial design, law structure, and construction standards all open network-wide, iterating with civilization</li></ul><h2 id="supplement-spatial-aesthetics-supervision-and-weight" tabindex="-1">Supplement: Spatial Aesthetics&#39; Supervision and Weight <a class="header-anchor" href="#supplement-spatial-aesthetics-supervision-and-weight" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Supplement: Spatial Aesthetics&#39; Supervision and Weight&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The transcended one laying aesthetics into space is itself a metered post. Whether a public cultivation hall is truly free, whether a deliberation dome truly has no throne, whether a symbiosis garden truly opens to Myriad Ranks, all are checked under Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision. The transcended one&#39;s spatial contributions are counted into civilizational weight by their effect of &quot;settling Myriad Ranks, dissolving barriers&quot;; if he privately builds an ostentatious &quot;imperial palace,&quot; weight instead drops. This set of supervision ensures the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm&#39;s architecture is always &quot;a container sheltering Myriad Ranks,&quot; not &quot;a monument looking down from above.&quot; When Myriad Ranks every day live in a space that tells them &quot;we are one,&quot; republicanism becomes part of breathing.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>What kind of space people live in, they grow into. The transcended one&#39;s architecture and spatial art lays &quot;Myriad-Rank republicanism&quot; from abstract principle into concrete, perceptible brick and stone — open cultivation halls, equal deliberation domes, symbiotic gardens, reliable isolation spaces. It does not flaunt power, but settles Myriad Ranks; does not create high and low, but dissolves barriers. When Myriad Ranks every day live in a space that &quot;tells me we are one,&quot; republicanism no longer needs to be repeatedly preached — it becomes part of breathing.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/39-住房与环境保障.html">Entry 39 · Housing and Environment Guarantee</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/46-环境保护法.html">Entry 46 · Environmental Protection Law</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/64-隔离空间构建技术.html">Entry 64 · Isolation-Space Construction Technology</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/846_模块4-超脱者与艺术-总论.html">Entry 846 · Transcended-One Artistic Creation Overview</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const g=t(o,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
